================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
================================================================================

VIGÍA is an integration project. It does not claim novel detection
architectures. Our contribution is the gated pipeline and the temporal
validation layer around these models.

Three of the five detectors are third-party weights and the work below is
theirs. Two — flood segmentation and building access — were trained by us, but
only in the sense that we fine-tuned someone else's architecture on someone
else's data: the architectures are torchvision's, the annotations are ATLANTIS's
and DRespNeT's, and both credits are recorded below and carry the same weight
as the rest.

Model weights are NOT redistributed in this repository. They are downloaded
from their original distributors by `tools/fetch_models.py`. Provenance,
licence and measured performance for each are recorded in models/REGISTRY.yaml.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. PyroNear — wildfire smoke detector
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Authors  : The PyroNear association — https://pyronear.org
Model    : yolo11s_sensitive-detector
Source   : https://huggingface.co/pyronear/yolo11s_sensitive-detector
Licence  : Apache-2.0 (as stated by the model repository)
Used for : Fire and smoke detection (vigia/detectors/fire.py)
Changes  : None to the model. We run the published ONNX export unmodified.
           We relabel its single class from "item" to "smoke" for readability
           downstream, and wrap it in our own pre/post-processing.

Licence note, recorded for transparency: the ONNX artifact carries an embedded
metadata field `license = AGPL-3.0 License (https://ultralytics.com/license)`,
stamped automatically by the Ultralytics exporter because the model was
fine-tuned from yolo11s.pt. The distributing repository states Apache-2.0. This
tension exists in PyroNear's own distribution and was not created by us. We
follow the licence the distributor states and record the discrepancy rather
than hiding it. We do not redistribute the weights in any case.

