5. DRespNeT — post-earthquake search-and-rescue dataset
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Authors  : Cranfield University
Source   : https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.16016
Licence  : CC BY 4.0
Used for : Training data for the building-access detector — UAV imagery of the
           2023 Turkiye earthquakes, 28 operationally critical classes covering
           collapsed structures, access points, debris, rescue personnel and
           civilian visibility. VIGIA merges these to five classes; see
           models/REGISTRY.yaml for the mapping and the reasoning.
Condition: CC BY 4.0 REQUIRES attribution. This differs from SeaDronesSee (CC0),
           where the credit below is given by choice rather than obligation.
           Any published figure, metric or weight file derived from DRespNeT
           must carry this credit. Because the licence expressly permits
           derivative works with attribution, weights trained on it MAY be
           redistributed provided this notice travels with them.

