6. ATLANTIS — waterbody semantic segmentation dataset
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Authors  : Erfani et al., iWERS laboratory, University of South Carolina
Source   : https://github.com/smhassanerfani/atlantis
Published: Environmental Modelling & Software, 2022
Licence  : NOT STATED — see condition below
Used for : Training data for the flood segmentation detector. 5,195
           pixel-annotated images, 56 classes, split 3,364 / 535 / 1,296,
           collapsed by us to binary water.
Condition: The repository carries NO explicit licence file, so the status of
           the annotations is unstated. We therefore do not redistribute the
           dataset, and whether weights trained on those annotations may be
           redistributed is genuinely unclear. That uncertainty is recorded
           rather than resolved in our favour. The source images were collected
           via the Flickr API under Creative Commons, No Known Copyright
           Restrictions, and US Government Work licences.

